## File: lambda-code/lambda_function.py

### Optional but Recommended: Add error handling around AppConfig call (Line ~108)
Replace:
```python
def get_application_features():
    url = f'http://localhost:2772/applications/cost-anomaly-to-slack-application/environments/cost-anomaly-to-slack-environment/configurations/cost-anomaly-to-slack-configuration-profile'
    config = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read()
    return config
```

With:
```python
def get_application_features():
    url = f'http://localhost:2772/applications/cost-anomaly-to-slack-application/environments/cost-anomaly-to-slack-environment/configurations/cost-anomaly-to-slack-configuration-profile'
    try:
        config = urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=10).read()
        return config
    except Exception as e:
        print(f"Error retrieving AppConfig: {e}")
        # Return default configuration if AppConfig fails
        return b'{"feature-flags": {"displayAccountName": false}}'
```

## Summary
These are the MINIMUM changes needed to make the 2021 code work in 2025:
1. Update Python runtime to 3.12
2. Fix AppConfig IAM permissions 
3. Update AppConfig layer ARNs to current versions
4. (Optional) Add basic error handling to prevent failures

The complete updated files (deployment-updated.yml and lambda_function_updated.py) provide additional improvements but these patches will restore basic functionality.
